From 7cf92d9d2bd73a67c84067f671a937107daa4313 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: medusa build <build@medusa.local>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 04:33:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(wallet): make pyo3/keycard_wallet an opt-in cargo
 feature

wallet-lez links libpython purely for Status Keycard support, which patch
0001 already disables at the CLI dispatch level. pyo3-ffi emits
`-lpython3.X` for the CPython of whatever machine ran the build, and the
live `Python::attach` call in account_manager.rs survives --gc-sections /
--as-needed, so the shipped binary records a hard dependency on that exact
CPython minor version:

  linux : `libpython3.10.so.1.0: cannot open shared object file`
  macOS : `dyld: Library not loaded: /Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/
           Versions/3.14/Python`

This fails at process-load time, before main(), so EVERY wallet subcommand
dies - including `account new public`, which is what the "Create your wallet"
dialog runs. Reported as paradoxcomputer/medusa#1.

Put `pyo3` and `keycard_wallet` behind a new, non-default `keycard` feature
and cfg-gate the five keycard call sites. With the feature off the binary has
no libpython dependency at all; `keycard`/`keycard-debug` builds are
unchanged. Cargo.lock is untouched (optional deps stay in the lock file).

Behaviour with the feature off:
  - `wallet keycard ...`          -> "Keycard is not supported in this build"
  - an `m/...` key-path account   -> clean error instead of a keycard prompt
  - signing with a keycard state  -> hard error, never a silently under-signed
                                     signature set
